<title>USA: Correctional Services stake cut by group.</title>
<headline>Correctional Services stake cut by group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group including New York-based Zweig-DiMenna Associates said Wednesday it has reduced its stake in Correctional Services Corp to 6.3 percent or 485,800 shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it most recently sold 92,500 shares of the Sarasota, Fla., company that provides staffing services to prisons between June 20 and July 14 at $11.77 to $13.25 a share.</p>
</text>
